  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 218 PM EDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nThese lovely dry conditions are coming to an end friday night as the \nnext frontal system pushes into the state just before daybreak Sat. \nFri morning a closed low center begins to deepen over KS as it \npushes into MO Fri afternoon/evening. Its trailing cold front pushes \nthrough the Mid/Southern MS river valley Fri night and begins \nknocking on NW GA's doorstep just before day break Sat. By Sat \nmorning The main low pressure center moves NE into the central Great \nlake states and into the Mid Atlantic/New England states Sun/Mon. \nThe frontal boundary on the other hand stalls across E/SE GA and the \nCarolinas as a developing Bermuda ridge blocks it from moving off \nshore. With GA on the periferia of this Ridge it will keep us in \nmoist SWLY flow through day 7. This will keep precipitation chances \nelevated with a diurnally driven trend each day. With showers and \nthunderstorms expected each day, highs temps will only get up into \nthe 80s to near 90 Sun through Wed.",
